	"history": "Far to the south, Ramesses II had two temples cut into the cliffs at Abu Simbel, with four seated colossi of himself at the door; he was not, it must be said, a modest king. And yet the temples are not quite where he left them! In the 1960s they were sawn into great blocks and raised onto higher ground, out of reach of the rising Lake Nasser.",
